  <!-- Rock Physics Analysis -->
  <section class="section section-dark" id="rock-physics">
    <div class="container-wide">
      <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-16 items-center">
        <div>
          <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-accent-500/10 text-xs font-medium text-accent-400 uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">
            Service
          </div>
          <h2 class="heading-lg mb-6">Rock Physics Analysis</h2>
          <p class="body-lg mb-6">
            Rock physics provides the theoretical link between reservoir properties (what we want to know) and seismic response (what we measure). This is the scientific foundation that makes quantitative interpretation possible.
          </p>
          <p class="body-md mb-8">
            We apply established theoretical models, calibrated to your specific geological setting, to understand how changes in porosity, fluid content, or lithology will manifest in seismic data.
          </p>
          
          <a href="/software" class="btn-primary">
            Explore SeisTool Software
            <svg class="w-4 h-4 ml-2" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
              <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10.293 3.293a1 1 0 011.414 0l6 6a1 1 0 010 1.414l-6 6a1 1 0 01-1.414-1.414L14.586 11H3a1 1 0 110-2h11.586l-4.293-4.293a1 1 0 010-1.414z" clip-rule="evenodd"/>
            </svg>
          </a>
        </div>
        
        <div class="card p-8">
          <h3 class="heading-sm mb-6">Theoretical Framework</h3>
          <div class="space-y-4">
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-navy-900/50 border-l-4 border-accent-500">
              <h4 class="font-semibold text-white text-sm mb-2">Gassmann Fluid Substitution</h4>
              <p class="text-navy-400 text-xs">
                Predicts how bulk modulus changes with pore fluid composition at low frequencies. The foundation for DHI analysis and time-lapse interpretation.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-navy-900/50 border-l-4 border-primary-500">
              <h4 class="font-semibold text-white text-sm mb-2">Hertz-Mindlin Contact Theory</h4>
              <p class="text-navy-400 text-xs">
                Models pressure-dependent elastic properties of granular media. Essential for understanding seismic velocity changes with depth and effective stress.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-navy-900/50 border-l-4 border-accent-400">
              <h4 class="font-semibold text-white text-sm mb-2">Hashin-Shtrikman Bounds</h4>
              <p class="text-navy-400 text-xs">
                Theoretical limits on effective elastic moduli for composite materials. Provides physics-based constraints on mixing relationships.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-navy-900/50 border-l-4 border-primary-400">
              <h4 class="font-semibold text-white text-sm mb-2">Inclusion Models (Kuster-Toksoz, DEM)</h4>
              <p class="text-navy-400 text-xs">
                Account for pore geometry effects on elastic properties. Critical for carbonates and fractured reservoirs where pore shape matters.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
